 #:seon.task{:name "a-firing-is-written-once-per-nominal-instant"
             :intent "Card C1. One clock proc in the cluster graph derives due instants from every task with `:seon.task/cron` (same cron library), writes one `:seon.task.fire/*` fact per [task nominal-at], and calls a task's `:seon.task/function` recording its result; replaces the per-agent timer and listener of `seon.schedule/schedule-step`. Read `seon.schedule/fire-due!`, `seon.schedule/next-nominal-after` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/runtime-follows-db.md`."}
 #:seon.task{:name "a-firing-to-a-live-agent-is-a-wake-and-to-none-an-attempt"
             :intent "Card C2. A firing of a cron task without a function: when the task's agent has a graph in the registry the firing is a listened fact (`:seon.task.fire/to`) and its wake; otherwise an attempt child by identity [task fire-at] that the reconciler launches; a refused delivery (`seon.cluster.wake/delivery`) writes the problem task. Read `seon.cluster.wake/route!`, `seon.schedule/fire-due!` and `docs/research/agent-platform/2026-10-11/runtime-follows-db.md`."}
